{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "15", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "04", "M": "18", "S": "16"}}, "news": [{"title": "After Mumbai, Pune set for plot-wise ready reckoner rates under micro-zoning", "para": "Pune and Mumbai are set to implement a detailed property valuation system that will transition from broad zoning classifications to more specific rates tied to individual plots and buildings. The state registration department is gearing up to adjust property rates for the upcoming year while introducing reforms like new stamp duty offices and mandatory land measurement. Additionally, linking Aadhaar may be required for all document registrations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/after-mumbai-pune-set-for-plot-wise-ready-reckoner-rates-under-micro-zoning/133254987?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-76444/133254987.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Gujarat government mulls higher FSI, taller buildings in GIDCs", "para": "The Gujarat government is set to enhance the floor space index for industrial plots located within GIDC estates. Building height regulations will be adjusted based on road width, permitting taller constructions. This initiative is designed to support vertical growth in several manufacturing industries. Industry representatives have persistently called for these updates in response to evolving economic realities, and the proposed changes invite public feedback for consideration.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/gujarat-government-mulls-higher-fsi-taller-buildings-in-gidcs/133254952?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-235520/133254952.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "SRA targets over five lakh rehabilitation homes by 2030, plans 19 cluster redevelopments in Mumbai", "para": "The SRA has set an ambitious goal to construct over 500,000 homes by the end of 2030. To facilitate this, annual targets will hasten slum redevelopment initiatives throughout the area. Innovations like amnesty programs and collaborative models are introduced for projects that have stalled. Additionally, a digital framework and computerized systems will enhance operational efficiency, while the Dharavi redevelopment is advancing through three distinct phases.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/sra-targets-over-five-lakh-rehabilitation-homes-by-2030-plans-19-cluster-redevelopments-in-mumbai/133254807?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-295612/133254807.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}